{{also|ljuga|leogan|ljúğa}}
==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|ljúga||to lie}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*leuganą}}, from {{der|is|ine-pro|*lewgʰ-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈljuːa/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|uːa|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|laug|lugu|logið}}

# {{lb|is|ambitransitive|governs the dative}} to [[lie]], to tell [[lies]] [about something]
#* Colossians 3:9
#*: '''''Ljúgið''' ekki hver að öðrum, því þér hafið afklæðst hinum gamla manni með gjörðum hans.''
#*:: Do not '''lie''' to each other, since you have taken off your old self with its practices.
#: {{ux|is|Hún '''lýgur''' alltaf að mér.|She's always '''lying''' to me.}}
#: {{ux|is|Ertu að '''ljúga'''?|Are you '''lying'''?}}
#: {{ux|is|Að '''ljúga''' til nafns.|To '''lie''' about one's name.}}
#: {{ux|is|Hún '''laug''' því að honum að hún væri ógift.|She '''lied''' to him about being unmarried.}}
#: {{ux|is|Ég er á þrettán bíla. — Þú '''lýgur''' því!|I own thirteen cars. — That's a '''lie'''!}}
#: {{ux|is|Hann lýgur því að hann eigi bíl.|He's '''lying''' about having a car.}}
# {{lb|is|transitive|governs the accusative}} to [[lie]] to someone, to tell [[lies]] to someone
#: ''Stjórnmálamenn hafa [[ljúga fullan|'''logið''' þig fullan]]!''
#:: Politicians have filled you with '''lies'''!
# {{lb|is|transitive|governs the dative}} to [[lie]] about something, to tell [[lies]] about something

